            <ArticleTitle>[Risk factors and coronary heart disease prevention in selected Lódź population--part II].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>749-53</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="THE AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Evaluation of the knowledge on CHD risk factors in selected Lódź population was made.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIAL AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">Realization of primary and secondary CHD prevention principles was assessed.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Over 20% of patients with CHD and over 38% of subjects without CHD did not realize the prevention principles. Hypolipemic therapy was effective only in 44.21% of patients with CHD and 35.9% of subjects without CHD. Antihypertensive therapy was successful in about 55% of patients with CHD and 35% of subjects without CHD.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The results of our study have shown low effectiveness of both CHD prevention principles realization and hipolipemic and antihypertensive therapy in selected Lódź population.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
